@{ ViewData["Title"] = "Privacy"; }
<section class="auth-shell"><article class="auth-card profile-card"><span class="eyebrow">Plain-language privacy</span><h1>Your practice data stays private</h1><p>BudgetBasics is an educational website. It does not perform banking transactions and must not be used to submit bank details, card numbers, passwords, or other sensitive financial information.</p><h2>What is stored</h2><p>If you create an optional account, SQL Server stores your display name, email, password hash, role, hashed refresh-session records, and expense-planner rows that you choose to save. Feedback submissions are also stored so the project can be improved. Raw passwords and raw refresh tokens are never stored.</p><h2>BudgetBee questions</h2><p>BudgetBee securely processes the text you enter to produce an educational answer. BudgetBasics does not permanently store chatbot questions. Do not enter bank details, card numbers, passwords, identification numbers, or private account information. A built-in educational guide remains available if a full response cannot be produced.</p><h2>What is not stored</h2><p>The 50-30-20 input, savings-goal figures, anonymous expense-planner rows, and chatbot questions are not permanently stored. Anonymous expense rows are cleared when the page is refreshed.</p><h2>Educational disclaimer</h2><p>All calculations and assistant answers are simplified learning information. They are not professional financial, legal, banking, investment, or tax advice.</p><a class="btn btn-primary" asp-action="Index">Return home</a></article></section>
